Also, over the last year and a half while doing Spork I've re-confirmed
one tautology; you can please some of the people all of the time, and
most of the people some of the time, but never all of the people all of
the time, and some of the people never.

If you're intending to do something along these lines, I would certainly
suggest just going ahead and doing it, and taking RGRN's collective 
opinion with some salt; you will surely get a number of responses from people
who fear change in any form, and who will select some individual thing
in your list as being a Holy Feature that Must Never Be Altered because
It Is Perfect.  To this I say "fuck 'em"; it's always possible to change
something back if it actually doesn't work well.  That's what "svn
revert" is for; replace with source versioning tool of your choice.  But
in the end, if you don't _try_ the change, you won't actually know
whether it was a good or bad idea.

Basically, consider that RGRN is by far _the_ most conservative part of the
Nethack (and roguelike) community, and listen accordingly.  :)

